// @name: 04 — Scene selector
// @tagline: named selectable scenes — pick calm or full live
// @description: One self-contained `.bps` with sections guarded by a flag (`flag section:1`): `1` calm (drums_r only) and `2` full (drums_r + lead_r). Open it and look at the code to see how the flag picks which rule derives. Ctrl+. to hush.
// @language: strudel
// @outputs: audio
// @level: intermediate
// @tags: scenes, select
// @showcase
//
// Sélecteur de scènes A5 — règles gardées par le drapeau `section`.
// section — 1 : calm, batterie seule · 2 : full, batterie + lead
flag section:1

actor drums  eval.strudel
actor lead  eval.strudel

-----
[section==1] S -> drums_r
[section==2] S -> { drums_r, lead_r }

drums_r -> drums.`note("c2*4").s("sine").gain(0.6)`
lead_r  -> lead.`note("e4 g4 b4 d5").s("triangle").gain(0.5)`
